-- #1111 A-2.6, the AMBIGUITY mirror: the record literal here is genuinely
-- undecidable, and must stay REJECTED.
--
-- A-2.6's whole argument is that a unit's own IMPORT SCOPE picks which module a bare
-- record/constructor name means.  That argument has a precondition — the scope must
-- name exactly one.  Here it names two: both `Cfg`s are imported BY NAME, so no
-- amount of import-scoping can choose, and the correct answer is a diagnostic rather
-- than either record.
--
-- ⚠️ The rejection is PRE-EXISTING and A-2.6 does not move it (verified first-hand:
-- byte-identical diagnostics on a binary built from pristine 40756bea and on A-2.6).
-- It is pinned here anyway because before this fixture it was pinned NOWHERE.  Derive
-- that rather than trust it — against the base commit, so this fixture's own
-- `oracle.json` does not answer the question it is asking:
--
--     git grep -l "brought into scope by both" 40756bea -- test/
--
-- returns exactly one path, `must_fail_fixtures/1253-…/claim.txt` — i.e. the
-- diagnostic was described in a claim about a DIFFERENT open bug and asserted by no
-- gate.  A widening of the overlay that started answering this from load order
-- instead would have had nothing to fail.
import arboth.{Cfg}
import zrboth.{Cfg}

v : Cfg
v = Cfg { fld = 7 }

main : <IO> Unit
main = println v.fld
